        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "dee4d4d7-a425-57f3-a5ec-0410d30b8da8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Times Square, Manhattan, New York City, West 45th Street, Central Park\n- Buildings: Bertelsmann Building, 1540 Broadway, 432 Park Avenue, One57, Loew's State Theatre\n- Topics: skyscraper heights, building completion, site replacement\n\nFacts:\n- Loew's State Theatre in New York City closed on February 19, 1987, and the Bertelsmann Building now occupies its site.\n- The former Bertelsmann Building is now known as 1540 Broadway.\n- 1540 Broadway is a 44-story, 733-foot office tower in Times Square in Manhattan, New York City, at West 45th Street.\n- 432 Park Avenue was originally proposed in 2011 to be 1,300 feet tall, but the structure topped out at 1,396 feet.\n- One57 was completed in 2014 at 1,005 feet tall and became New York City's tallest residential building for a few months until 432 Park Avenue was completed.\n- 432 Park Avenue is a residential skyscraper in New York City that overlooks Central Park.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "5b92787e-0560-52db-9f65-db1144587bae",
        "text": "Page: Bertelsmann Building. Sentence: The former Bertelsmann Building, now known as 1540 Broadway, is a 44-story, 733 foot (223 m) office tower in Times Square in Manhattan, New York City, standing at West 45th Street.\nPage: 432 Park Avenue. Sentence: 432 Park Avenue is a residential skyscraper in New York City that overlooks Central Park.\nPage: 432 Park Avenue. Sentence: Originally proposed to be 1300 ft in 2011, the structure topped out at 1396 ft .\nPage: Loew's State Theatre (New York City). Sentence: It closed on February 19, 1987, and it is now the site of the Bertelsmann Building.\nPage: One57. Sentence: Upon completion in 2014, it stood at 1,005 ft tall, making it the tallest residential building in the city for a few months until the completion of 432 Park Avenue.",
